mindmap
  root((Build Your Own AI Software Factory with Claude Code))
    Goals
      Learn what a software factory is
      Build your own in a real, working project
    What is a software factory?
      The earliest well-documented ancestor is Robert W. Bemer at General Electric in 1968
      essentially a computer-controlled programming environment
      containing standardized development tools
      along with historical information
      for management and measurement
    A short history
      1968 - The idea is proposed
        Bob Bemer - a factory to boost programmer productivity with standardized tools and data for management controls
      1969 - Hitachi opens the first software factory
        A whole software organization run like a factory
        Goal - high-quality software in great quantity
      2000s - Factory as an assembly kit
        Apps assembled from reusable patterns, models, and frameworks
      2010s-2020s - Factory as a delivery pipeline
        People, tools, and processes for continuous delivery
        CI/CD, automated tests, security checks
      Now - Agentic factories
        AI agents plan, write, test, and review the code
    Agentic software factory 101
      What is new is automation of relatively unstructured cognitive work between the deterministic stages
      trigger, sandbox, agent, checks, PR, human merge
      Triggers
        GitHub issues, Linear/Jira tickets, Slack messages, cron schedules
        Incidents and error alerts - e.g. Sentry
      Diagnostics pulled in automatically
        Stack traces, logs, metrics, and affected releases handed to the agent - e.g. Sentry over MCP
      Isolation
        A fresh sandbox per run - clones the repo, destroyed when done
        Lets many agents work in parallel
      Verification
        The repo's own tests and checks, plus code and secret scanning
        A real browser can drive UI changes
      Pull request
        The diff plus evidence - test results, traces, a preview environment
      Human gates
        Approve the spec before code exists
        Approve the merge before it ships
      Audit trail
        Every agent session and tool call is saved
      In the wild
        About 30% of merged PRs at Ramp come from its internal agent
        11% of PRs at Uber are opened by agents
    Claude Code demo
      Build a software factory inside my zazencodes.com codebase
    Our simple agentic software factory
      A team of AI agents that takes a feature from idea to merged code
      Each agent has one job
        Write the spec
        Build it
        Review it
        Approve it
    The factory line
      Spec writer Opus, Builder Opus, 4 reviews in parallel, Approver Opus
      CHANGES - orchestrator resumes builder, max 2
      Low risk - Merge to main
      Escalate - Needs human, /factory approve
    The orchestrator
      One Claude Code session runs the /factory skill and becomes the orchestrator
      Runs the loop
      Spawns every agent
      Only writer of factory/board.json
    Files hold the state
      Agents get context from files, not the conversation
      Each agent writes only its own file
    The dashboard
      Jobs are cards moving across the loop's stages
      Each review round shows as a row of reviewer chips that fill in as verdicts land
      needs-human jobs stand out
      Click a card to read its markdown files
    1. Build the factory
      Paste the build prompt into Claude Code
      A Claude Code skill, subagents, and markdown files
      Keep it small - a viewer should understand the whole thing in a few minutes
    2. Run the factory
      /factory my obsidian agent setup course pages should not be paywalled, ONLY the videos are paywalled
      Spec writer drafts the spec, Opus
      Builder builds it on a feature branch, Opus
      4 reviewers run in parallel, 1 Opus, 3 Sonnet
      Approver merges to main, or sends the job to needs-human
    Commands
      /factory feature - run a new job through the loop
      /factory next - run the first unchecked item in backlog.md
      /factory approve job-id - merge a needs-human job into main
      /factory rework job-id note - send a job back to the builder with feedback
    Limitations and next steps
      Git worktrees added so several jobs run in parallel
      GitHub Issues as input, or a trigger from Slack
      Connect app metrics, e.g. Sentry, so production bugs flow in with context
      Watch after deploy - roll back a shipped feature that breaks something
